# Tool caches. `lint-imports` writes .import_linter_cache/ at the repo root and
# Prettier does not honour the nested .gitignore Grimp puts inside it, so
# `make lint-py` would otherwise make the later `prettier --check .` fail.
.import_linter_cache/

# Build output. `fdp-manual-build build --html-only` and `make manual-html`
# write the assembled variants here. It is ignored by the nested
# tools/manual-build/.gitignore, which Prettier does not read either.
tools/manual-build/.build/

# Hand-formatted Markdown: Prettier would realign the tables.
CHANGELOG.md
README.md
# The evaluation records are committed as written: the held-out seal test reads
# the seal's hash lines, the harness parses the choice record's NAME=value lines,
# and the final-run record is a fixed account of one run.
tools/eval/records/**

# Manual source of truth. manual/build.yaml and the spec YAML keep their flow
# style verbatim, and manual/spec/derived/*.json is written by
# manual/tools/derive_bands.py with
# json.dumps(indent=2, sort_keys=True) — Prettier reflows both, which would make
# the band derivation irreproducible. The test fixtures mirror those files.
manual/build.yaml
manual/spec/**/*.yaml
manual/spec/derived/**
manual/tools/tests/fixtures/**
tools/manual-build/tests/fixtures/**

# The init fixtures, for the same reason. `contracts/**` holds byte copies
# of `packages/contracts/**` that `test_contracts_drift.py` compares with
# `read_bytes()`, and one of them, `contracts/embedding.json`, copies a file
# Prettier is already told to leave alone below. `mini-manual/mini-manual.html`
# is the single source of the two committed PDFs, whose pagination
# `expected.json` pins and `build.sh --check` re-verifies, so reflowing its
# markup would move the page breaks the extractor tests assert.
tools/init/tests/fixtures/**

# Build output of `fdp-manual-build build`, written with
# json.dumps(indent=2, sort_keys=True) so its bytes are a function of the
# manual sources. Prettier collapses the short arrays, which would leave the
# tree dirty after every `make manual`.
tools/eval/fixtures/catalog.json

# The embedding pin and its reference fixture, written by
# packages/contracts/scripts/embed_fixture.py with json.dumps(indent=2). Prettier
# collapses `onnx.inputs` onto one line and refills the 384-component vectors, so
# every `pnpm --filter @fdp/contracts embed-fixture` run would leave the tree dirty
# and the pin would stop being a function of the model files.
packages/contracts/embedding.json
packages/contracts/fixtures/embeddings/**

# The backend's calibration fixture of the manual's catalog, written by
# tools/eval/scripts/export-man-fixture.ts with JSON.stringify(sorted, null, 2).
# tools/eval/test/man-fixture-drift.test.ts compares it with a fresh export, and
# Prettier would collapse the short arrays and leave the tree dirty after every
# export.
apps/backend/test/fixtures/catalog/man/catalog.json

# The golden Von request and its reported tokens. The test compares the file
# byte for byte with JSON.stringify(body, null, 2) of the request the SDK
# sent, and `vitest -u` rewrites it that way; Prettier collapses the short
# arrays, which would break the comparison and leave the tree dirty.
apps/backend/test/fixtures/von/*.json
